  "body": "From the review of PR #82 (#77). Nothing compares the drill's flute length with the hole depth measured from the raw surface. On radial (cross) programs the verify laws stand down (until #79 lands) and only the fixture laws remain, so with a short flute the shank or holder feeds into uncut stock with no warning - a collision. PR #82 makes it much more likely: holes now start at the raw surface, ~16 mm deep in the test against ~6 mm before. Axial drilling should be checked for the same gap.\n\nDone means: every drilling op (cross and axial) refuses by name a hole deeper, from the raw/stock surface, than the tool's usable flute length (and flags shank-in-stock), pinned by a short-drill test on raw stock wider than the part.",
